{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אנשים אשר היו טמאים לנפש אדם", :translit "anashim asher hayu temei'im le-nefesh adam", :gloss "men who were defiled by the dead body of a man"} {:he "אלו שהיו נושאין ארונו של יוסף", :translit "elu she-hayu nos'in arono shel yosef", :gloss "these are those who carried the coffin of Joseph"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אנשים אשר היו טמאים לנפש אדם", :b "אלו שהיו נושאין ארונו של יוסף"}], :frame {:text "When Joseph died, he had his brothers swear that God would visit them and they would carry his bones up from Egypt (Genesis 50:25). Moses took the bones of Joseph with him (Exodus 13:19), and the Israelites carried Joseph's bones for burial in Shechem (Joshua 24:32). The midrashic tradition identifies these specific men as prominent figures, sometimes named as Levi's sons or the sons of Joseph's brothers, who were occupied with carrying Joseph's coffin and therefore could not bring the Passover offering at its appointed time (Sotah 13a; Tanchuma, Tzav 14).", :sources ["Genesis 50:25" "Exodus 13:19" "Joshua 24:32" "Sotah 13a" "Tanchuma, Tzav 14"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אשר היו טמאים", :translit "asher hayu temei'im", :gloss "who were defiled"} {:he "מת מצוה", :translit "met mitzvah", :gloss "a deceased person lacking burial"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אשר היו טמאים", :b "זה למת מצוה"}], :frame {:text "A 'met mitzvah' is a deceased person who has no one else to bury him; in such a case even a nazir, who is ordinarily forbidden to contract corpse-impurity, is commanded to become impure and bury the dead (Nazir 43b; Sotah 14b). The Sifrei (Bamidbar 7:1) explains that the men in Numbers 9:6 had become impure on account of burying a met mitzvah, and because this impurity was acquired through the performance of a mitzvah, they approached Moses asking why they should be penalized and excluded from the Passover offering.", :sources ["Nazir 43b" "Sotah 14b" "Sifrei Bamidbar 7:1"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "אנשים אשר היו טמאים לנפש אדם", :a-value 1528, :b "אלו שהיו נושאין ארונו של יוסף", :b-value 1524, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:a-value 622, :b-value 623, :lens :standard, :equal? false, :kind :gematria, :b "זה למת מצוה", :by :selah, :colel? true, :a "אשר היו טמאים"}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:27:57.035363909Z", :model "glm-5.2"}